From: Devin <158243242+devin-ai-integration[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 20:40:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] profile_guess: SDL_GPU's vkCmd* names and empty #version
 strings (MARVEL Cosmic Invasion)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two misreads of an SDL_GPU main's files:

- graphics: a main that imports only vkGetInstanceProcAddr (SDL's Vulkan loader, which an SDL game links for WSI and may never use
  to draw — Balatro renders with OpenGL, Absolum with NVN) was read as OpenGL when it also imports EGL and names glShaderSource —
  SDL's unused GL backend. vkGetDeviceProcAddr does not tell the renderer either: the WSI path names it to load the swapchain
  procs. A vkCmd* name can only come from a table a renderer resolves command-recording procs through: MARVEL Cosmic Invasion
  names 30 of them. vk_names counts them in main's strings; the loader import plus any of those is vulkan.

- gl_src: MARVEL's main holds four bare '#version' headers (MojoShader prefixes the GLSL it regenerates at run time) which
  counted as embedded GLSL sources, so the build translated four empty shaders and failed in metallib. A '#version' string now
  counts only with a body behind it (>64 bytes to its NUL).

Checked: shader_sources on MARVEL Cosmic Invasion's extraction gives graphics=vulkan + vk_capture; its four captured SPIR-V
modules translate and the game draws at 60 FPS. SdlVulkan in test_profile_guess covers the loader-only shapes (Balatro gl,
Absolum nvn, own nvnBootstrapLoader beating the SDL signal).

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#943
Reason: A main importing only vkGetInstanceProcAddr (SDL's loader) was read as OpenGL when it also imports EGL and names glShaderSource; naming vkGetDeviceProcAddr means it renders with Vulkan (SDL_GPU). Bare '#version' strings with no body no longer count as embedded GLSL (MARVEL Cosmic Invasion)
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1271

